.TH FLINK 1.SH NAMEflink \- make a second directory entry for a file.SH SYNOPSIS\fBflink\fRfile ....SH DESCRIPTION\fBflink\fRadds a directory entry, in the current directory, that points at thefile descriptor of each file named -- a hard link, in Unix terms.  RBFhas no hard links: it keeps no count of the entries pointing at a file,so removing either entry frees the file under the other..PPDo not use it on a disk you care about.  Removing a link it made hasbeen seen to leave the original entry pointing at a directory, afterwhich the file cannot be read by name.  Rebuild or restore the disk ifthat happens..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR